[38;2;124;124;124mActually, the issue is that each square can be parameterized in multiple ways [0m
[38;2;124;124;124m(different choices of which vertex is z1 and which direction w goes). So I [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mshouldn't just add up the counts from different sub-cases.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mLet me reconsider the approach. The key finding is:[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m1. Every square in P_n either has the origin as a vertex or is centered at the [0m
[38;2;124;124;124morigin.[0m
